IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb2-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), Part VII, sections 50 to 54 -- SECURITIES
-- REGISTERS; DEALINGS WITH THE REGISTERED HOLDER; OVERISSUE; BURDEN OF PROOF; FUNGIBLE SECURITIES. Layer 1.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Encoded from a plain-text rendering of the Justice Canada consolidation current to
-- 2026-09-30, which is not an official version; nothing here is verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RULE. Named `<what it works out> within s <section>`. A requirement ("shall maintain") is
-- encoded as a rule TRUE when it is met; a permission ("may") as TRUE when the conditions for it hold; a
-- bar ("is not required", "is not effective") as TRUE when the bar applies. Where a provision says what
-- follows in a stated case, the rule is TRUE when that case holds; FALSE means only that this provision
-- does not apply. A rule whose result is a MAYBE returns NOTHING where the text is silent for the case.
-- Within one module, a rule that depends on another section's rule calls it and takes its inputs; a plain
-- input stands in for another section only across modules, and says so ("out of range" or "to avoid a cycle").

§ `s 50 Securities records`

§§ `s 50(1) Securities register`

-- The register records the securities issued in registered form and shows, for each class or series,
-- (a) the names, alphabetically arranged, and latest known address of each person who is or has been a
-- security holder, (b) the number held by each, and (c) the date and particulars of each issue and transfer.
-- src:799 | Securities records
-- src:800 | 50 (1) A corporation shall maintain a securities register in which it records the securities issued by it in registered form, showing with respect to each class or series of securities
-- src:801 | (a) the names, alphabetically arranged, and the latest known address of each person who is or has been a security holder;
-- src:802 | (b) the number of securities held by each security holder; and
-- src:803 | (c) the date and particulars of the issue and transfer of each security.
@ref CBCA s 50(1) (src:799-803)
GIVEN `the register records the securities the corporation issued in registered form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class or series the register shows the names, alphabetically arranged, and the latest known address of each person who is or has been a security holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class or series the register shows the number of securities held by each security holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for each class or series the register shows the date and particulars of the issue and transfer of each security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation maintains the securities register as required within s 50(1)` MEANS
        `the register records the securities the corporation issued in registered form`
    AND `for each class or series the register shows the names, alphabetically arranged, and the latest known address of each person who is or has been a security holder`
    AND `for each class or series the register shows the number of securities held by each security holder`
    AND `for each class or series the register shows the date and particulars of the issue and transfer of each security`

§§ `s 50(2) Central and branch registers`

-- src:804 | Central and branch registers
-- src:805 | (2) A corporation may appoint an agent or mandatary to maintain a central securities register and branch securities registers.
@ref CBCA s 50(2) (src:804-805)
GIVEN `the person appointed is an agent or mandatary of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may appoint the person to maintain a central or branch securities register within s 50(2)` MEANS
    `the person appointed is an agent or mandatary of the corporation`

§§ `s 50(3) Place of register`

-- A central register is kept at the registered office or at any other place IN CANADA that the directors
-- designate; a branch register may be kept at any place in or out of Canada that the directors designate.
-- src:806 | Place of register
-- src:807 | (3) A central securities register shall be maintained by a corporation at its registered office or at any other place in Canada designated by the directors, and any branch securities registers may be kept at any place in or out of Canada designated by the directors.
@ref CBCA s 50(3) (src:806-807)
GIVEN `the central register is kept at the registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the central register is kept at another place in Canada designated by the directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the central securities register is kept at a permitted place within s 50(3)` MEANS
        `the central register is kept at the registered office of the corporation`
    OR  `the central register is kept at another place in Canada designated by the directors`

-- src:806 | Place of register
-- src:807 | (3) A central securities register shall be maintained by a corporation at its registered office or at any other place in Canada designated by the directors, and any branch securities registers may be kept at any place in or out of Canada designated by the directors.
@ref CBCA s 50(3) (src:806-807)
GIVEN `the branch register is kept at a place designated by the directors, in or out of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a branch securities register is kept at a permitted place within s 50(3)` MEANS
    `the branch register is kept at a place designated by the directors, in or out of Canada`

§§ `s 50(4) Effect of registration`

-- src:808 | Effect of registration
-- src:809 | (4) Registration of the issue or transfer of a security in the central securities register or in a branch securities register is complete and valid registration for all purposes.
@ref CBCA s 50(4) (src:808-809)
GIVEN `the issue or transfer is registered in the central securities register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the issue or transfer is registered in a branch securities register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the registration is complete and valid for all purposes within s 50(4)` MEANS
        `the issue or transfer is registered in the central securities register`
    OR  `the issue or transfer is registered in a branch securities register`

§§ `s 50(5) Branch register`

-- src:810 | Branch register
-- src:811 | (5) A branch securities register shall only contain particulars of securities issued or transferred at that branch.
@ref CBCA s 50(5) (src:810-811)
GIVEN `every particular in the branch register is of a security issued or transferred at that branch` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a branch securities register contains only what it may within s 50(5)` MEANS
    `every particular in the branch register is of a security issued or transferred at that branch`

§§ `s 50(6) Central register`

-- src:812 | Central register
-- src:813 | (6) Particulars of each issue or transfer of a security registered in a branch securities register shall also be kept in the corresponding central securities register.
@ref CBCA s 50(6) (src:812-813)
GIVEN `the particulars are registered in a branch securities register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the particulars are also kept in the corresponding central securities register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the particulars are also kept in the central securities register as required within s 50(6)` MEANS
        (NOT `the particulars are registered in a branch securities register`)
    OR  `the particulars are also kept in the corresponding central securities register`

§§ `s 50(7) Destruction of certificates`

-- The corporation, its agent or mandatary, or a trustee as defined in subsection 82(1), is not required to
-- produce (a) a cancelled certificate, a cancelled instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) (out of range:
-- section 29(1) (piece cb1)) or a like cancelled instrument, in registered form, six years after the date of its
-- cancellation; (b) the same, in bearer form, after the date of its cancellation; or (c) an instrument
-- referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument, irrespective of its form, after the date of its
-- expiration. The rule is TRUE when one of the three reliefs applies on the day asked about. FALSE means only
-- that s 50(7) does not relieve the corporation of producing it that day. The cancellation date is NOTHING
-- when the instrument has not been cancelled, and the expiration date is NOTHING when it has not expired
-- (or is not an instrument that expires).
-- src:814 | Destruction of certificates
-- src:815 | (7) A corporation, its agent or mandatary, or a trustee as defined in subsection 82(1) is not required to produce
-- src:816 | (a) a cancelled security certificate in registered form, an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) that is cancelled or a like cancelled instrument in registered form six years after the date of its cancellation;
-- src:817 | (b) a cancelled security certificate in bearer form or an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) that is cancelled or a like cancelled instrument in bearer form after the date of its cancellation; or
-- src:818 | (c) an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument, irrespective of its form, after the date of its expiration.
@ref CBCA s 50(7) (src:814-818)
DECLARE `Form of an instrument under s 50(7)` IS ONE OF
    `an instrument in registered form under s 50(7)`
    `an instrument in bearer form under s 50(7)`
    `an instrument in neither registered nor bearer form under s 50(7)`

-- src:814 | Destruction of certificates
-- src:815 | (7) A corporation, its agent or mandatary, or a trustee as defined in subsection 82(1) is not required to produce
-- src:816 | (a) a cancelled security certificate in registered form, an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) that is cancelled or a like cancelled instrument in registered form six years after the date of its cancellation;
-- src:817 | (b) a cancelled security certificate in bearer form or an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) that is cancelled or a like cancelled instrument in bearer form after the date of its cancellation; or
-- src:818 | (c) an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument, irrespective of its form, after the date of its expiration.
@ref CBCA s 50(7) (src:814-818)
GIVEN `the form of the instrument` IS A `Form of an instrument under s 50(7)`
      `the date the instrument was cancelled, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the instrument expired, if it is an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument that has expired` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation, its agent or a trustee need not produce the instrument within s 50(7)` MEANS
        (    `the form of the instrument` EQUALS `an instrument in registered form under s 50(7)`
         AND CONSIDER `the date the instrument was cancelled, if it was`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST c THEN `the day asked about` AT LEAST (`the last day of` (`Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 6, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`) `counted from` c))
    OR  (    `the form of the instrument` EQUALS `an instrument in bearer form under s 50(7)`
         AND CONSIDER `the date the instrument was cancelled, if it was`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST c THEN `the day asked about` GREATER THAN c)
    OR  CONSIDER `the date the instrument expired, if it is an instrument referred to in subsection 29(1) or a like instrument that has expired`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST e THEN `the day asked about` GREATER THAN e

§ `s 51 Dealings with registered holder`

§§ `s 51(1) Dealings with registered holder`

-- The corporation (or a trustee defined in subsection 82(1)) may treat the registered owner as the person
-- exclusively entitled to vote, to receive notices and payments and otherwise to exercise all the rights of
-- an owner, subject to sections 134, 135 and 138 (out of range: section 134 (piece cb3); section 135 (piece cb3); section 138 (piece cb3)).
-- src:819 | Dealings with registered holder
-- src:820 | 51 (1) A corporation or a trustee defined in subsection 82(1) may, subject to sections 134, 135 and 138, treat the registered owner of a security as the person exclusively entitled to vote, to receive notices, to receive any interest, dividend or other payments in respect of the security, and otherwise to exercise all the rights and powers of an owner of the security.
@ref CBCA s 51(1) (src:819-820)
GIVEN `the person is the registered owner of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 134, 135 or 138 limits the treatment of the registered owner as exclusively entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may treat the registered owner as exclusively entitled within s 51(1)` MEANS
        `the person is the registered owner of the security`
    AND (NOT `section 134, 135 or 138 limits the treatment of the registered owner as exclusively entitled`)

§§ `s 51(2) Constructive registered holder`

-- A corporation whose articles restrict the right to transfer its securities SHALL, and any other
-- corporation MAY, treat a person as a registered security holder entitled to exercise all the rights of
-- the security holder the person represents, if the person furnishes the evidence described in subsection
-- 77(4) (see `evidence of appointment or incumbency within s 77(4)` in cb2-part7-registration.l4) and is in
-- one of the capacities (a) to (c). NOTHING: the person is in none of the capacities, or furnishes no evidence.
-- src:821 | Constructive registered holder
-- src:822 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1), a corporation whose articles restrict the right to transfer its securities shall, and any other corporation may, treat a person as a registered security holder entitled to exercise all the rights of the security holder that the person represents, if the person furnishes the corporation with evidence as described in subsection 77(4) that the person is
-- src:823 | (a) the heir of a deceased security holder, or the personal representative of the heirs, or the personal representative of the estate or succession of a deceased security holder;
-- src:824 | (b) a personal representative of a registered security holder who is an infant, an incapable person or a missing person; or
-- src:825 | (c) a liquidator of, or a trustee in bankruptcy for, a registered security holder.
@ref CBCA s 51(2) (src:821-825)
DECLARE `Capacity of a person who claims for a security holder under s 51(2)` IS ONE OF
    `the heir of a deceased security holder`
    `the personal representative of the heirs of a deceased security holder`
    `the personal representative of the estate or succession of a deceased security holder`
    `a personal representative of a registered security holder who is an infant, an incapable person or a missing person`
    `a liquidator of a registered security holder`
    `a trustee in bankruptcy for a registered security holder`
    `a person in none of these capacities under s 51(2)`

DECLARE `What the corporation must or may do under s 51(2)` IS ONE OF
    `the corporation must treat the person as a registered security holder`
    `the corporation may treat the person as a registered security holder`

-- src:821 | Constructive registered holder
-- src:822 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1), a corporation whose articles restrict the right to transfer its securities shall, and any other corporation may, treat a person as a registered security holder entitled to exercise all the rights of the security holder that the person represents, if the person furnishes the corporation with evidence as described in subsection 77(4) that the person is
-- src:823 | (a) the heir of a deceased security holder, or the personal representative of the heirs, or the personal representative of the estate or succession of a deceased security holder;
-- src:824 | (b) a personal representative of a registered security holder who is an infant, an incapable person or a missing person; or
-- src:825 | (c) a liquidator of, or a trustee in bankruptcy for, a registered security holder.
@ref CBCA s 51(2) (src:821-825)
GIVEN `the articles of the corporation restrict the right to transfer its securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the capacity of the person` IS A `Capacity of a person who claims for a security holder under s 51(2)`
      `the person furnishes evidence as described in subsection 77(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `What the corporation must or may do under s 51(2)`
`whether the corporation must or may treat the person as a registered security holder within s 51(2)` MEANS
    IF     (`the capacity of the person` EQUALS `a person in none of these capacities under s 51(2)`)
        OR (NOT `the person furnishes evidence as described in subsection 77(4)`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the articles of the corporation restrict the right to transfer its securities`
         THEN JUST `the corporation must treat the person as a registered security holder`
         ELSE JUST `the corporation may treat the person as a registered security holder`

§§ `s 51(3) Permissible registered holder`

-- "other than a person described in subsection (2)": a person in one of the capacities of s 51(2)(a) to (c).
-- src:826 | Permissible registered holder
-- src:827 | (3) If a person on whom the ownership of a security devolves by operation of law, other than a person described in subsection (2), furnishes proof of the person’s authority to exercise rights or privileges in respect of a security of the corporation that is not registered in the person’s name, the corporation shall treat the person as entitled to exercise those rights or privileges.
@ref CBCA s 51(3) (src:826-827)
GIVEN `ownership of the security devolves on the person by operation of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the capacity of the person` IS A `Capacity of a person who claims for a security holder under s 51(2)`
      `the security is not registered in the person's name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person furnishes proof of their authority to exercise rights or privileges in respect of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must treat the person as entitled to exercise the rights within s 51(3)` MEANS
        `ownership of the security devolves on the person by operation of law`
    AND `the capacity of the person` EQUALS `a person in none of these capacities under s 51(2)`
    AND `the security is not registered in the person's name`
    AND `the person furnishes proof of their authority to exercise rights or privileges in respect of the security`

§§ `s 51(4) Immunity of corporation`

-- src:828 | Immunity of corporation
-- src:829 | (4) A corporation is not required to inquire into the existence of, or see to the performance or observance of, any duty owed to a third person by a registered holder of any of its securities or by anyone whom it treats, as permitted or required by this section, as the owner or registered holder thereof.
@ref CBCA s 51(4) (src:828-829)
GIVEN `the duty is owed to a third person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duty is owed by a registered holder of a security of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duty is owed by a person the corporation treats, as permitted or required by section 51, as the owner or registered holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation is not required to inquire into or see to the duty within s 51(4)` MEANS
        `the duty is owed to a third person`
    AND (   `the duty is owed by a registered holder of a security of the corporation`
         OR `the duty is owed by a person the corporation treats, as permitted or required by section 51, as the owner or registered holder`)

§§ `s 51(5) Persons less than 18 years of age`

-- If a person under 18 exercises any rights of ownership in the securities, no later repudiation, avoidance
-- or (in Quebec) annulment or reduction of obligations is effective against the corporation. TRUE when
-- such a later step is ineffective against the corporation.
-- src:830 | Persons less than 18 years of age
-- src:831 | (5) If a person who is less than 18 years of age exercises any rights of ownership in the securities of a corporation, no subsequent repudiation or avoidance or, in Quebec, annulment or reduction of obligations is effective against the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 51(5) (src:830-831)
GIVEN `the age in years of the person when they exercised rights of ownership in the securities` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a later repudiation, avoidance, annulment or reduction of obligations is ineffective against the corporation within s 51(5)` MEANS
    `the age in years of the person when they exercised rights of ownership in the securities` LESS THAN 18

§§ `s 51(6) Joint holders`

-- src:832 | Joint holders
-- src:833 | (6) A corporation may treat as owner of a security the survivors of persons to whom the security was issued as joint holders, if it receives proof satisfactory to it of the death of any such joint holder.
@ref CBCA s 51(6) (src:832-833)
GIVEN `the security was issued to persons as joint holders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation receives proof of the death of a joint holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is satisfied with the proof` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may treat the survivors as owner of the security within s 51(6)` MEANS
        `the security was issued to persons as joint holders`
    AND `the corporation receives proof of the death of a joint holder`
    AND `the corporation is satisfied with the proof`

§§ `s 51(7) Transmission of securities`

-- A person referred to in paragraph (2)(a): the heir of a deceased security holder, or the personal
-- representative of the heirs, or of the estate or succession. The rule below works it out from the capacity.
-- src:821 | Constructive registered holder
-- src:822 | (2) Notwithstanding subsection (1), a corporation whose articles restrict the right to transfer its securities shall, and any other corporation may, treat a person as a registered security holder entitled to exercise all the rights of the security holder that the person represents, if the person furnishes the corporation with evidence as described in subsection 77(4) that the person is
-- src:823 | (a) the heir of a deceased security holder, or the personal representative of the heirs, or the personal representative of the estate or succession of a deceased security holder;
@ref CBCA s 51(2)(a) (src:821-823)
GIVEN `the capacity of the person` IS A `Capacity of a person who claims for a security holder under s 51(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a) within s 51(2)` MEANS
        `the capacity of the person` EQUALS `the heir of a deceased security holder`
    OR  `the capacity of the person` EQUALS `the personal representative of the heirs of a deceased security holder`
    OR  `the capacity of the person` EQUALS `the personal representative of the estate or succession of a deceased security holder`

-- The documents s 51(7) requires to be deposited with the corporation or its transfer agent: (a) the
-- original grant of probate, letters of administration or (in Quebec) probate of the will or of the notarial
-- minutes, or a copy certified true by the court or notary, a trust company, or a lawyer or notary acting
-- for the person; or (b) in Quebec, in a transmission by notarial will, an authentic copy; together with (c)
-- an affidavit or declaration of transmission and (d) the deceased holder's security certificate (endorsed
-- under section 65 if the transfer is to anyone other than a paragraph (2)(a) person), accompanied by any
-- assurance the corporation may require under section 77.
-- src:834 | Transmission of securities
-- src:835 | (7) Subject to any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes, a person referred to in paragraph (2)(a) is entitled to become a registered holder, or to designate a registered holder, if the person deposits with the corporation or its transfer agent
-- src:836 | (a) the original grant of probate, of letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate, or a copy certified to be a true copy of one of those documents by
-- src:837 | (i) the court that granted the probate or letters of administration, or the notary who prepared the minutes of the probate,
-- src:838 | (ii) a trust company incorporated under the laws of Canada or a province, or
-- src:839 | (iii) a lawyer or notary acting on behalf of the person referred to in paragraph (2)(a), or
-- src:840 | (b) in the case of transmission by notarial will in Quebec, an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province,
-- src:841 | together with
-- src:842 | (c) an affidavit or declaration of transmission made by a person referred to in paragraph (2)(a), stating the particulars of the transmission, and
-- src:843 | (d) the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder
-- src:844 | (i) in case of a transfer to a person referred to in paragraph (2)(a), with or without the endorsement of that person, and
-- src:845 | (ii) in case of a transfer to any other person, endorsed in accordance with section 65,
-- src:846 | and accompanied by any assurance the corporation may require under section 77.
@ref CBCA s 51(7) (src:834-846)
GIVEN `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the documents required by subsection 51(7) have been deposited within s 51(7)` MEANS
        (   `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate`
         OR `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person`
         OR `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province`)
    AND `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission`
    AND `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder`
    AND (   `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)`
         OR `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65`)
    AND `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77`

-- Subject to any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes.
-- src:834 | Transmission of securities
-- src:835 | (7) Subject to any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes, a person referred to in paragraph (2)(a) is entitled to become a registered holder, or to designate a registered holder, if the person deposits with the corporation or its transfer agent
-- src:836 | (a) the original grant of probate, of letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate, or a copy certified to be a true copy of one of those documents by
-- src:837 | (i) the court that granted the probate or letters of administration, or the notary who prepared the minutes of the probate,
-- src:838 | (ii) a trust company incorporated under the laws of Canada or a province, or
-- src:839 | (iii) a lawyer or notary acting on behalf of the person referred to in paragraph (2)(a), or
-- src:840 | (b) in the case of transmission by notarial will in Quebec, an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province,
-- src:841 | together with
-- src:842 | (c) an affidavit or declaration of transmission made by a person referred to in paragraph (2)(a), stating the particulars of the transmission, and
-- src:843 | (d) the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder
-- src:844 | (i) in case of a transfer to a person referred to in paragraph (2)(a), with or without the endorsement of that person, and
-- src:845 | (ii) in case of a transfer to any other person, endorsed in accordance with section 65,
-- src:846 | and accompanied by any assurance the corporation may require under section 77.
@ref CBCA s 51(7) (src:834-846)
GIVEN `the capacity of the person` IS A `Capacity of a person who claims for a security holder under s 51(2)`
      `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes stands in the way` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is entitled to become or designate a registered holder within s 51(7)` MEANS
        `the person is a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a) within s 51(2)` `the capacity of the person`
    AND `the documents required by subsection 51(7) have been deposited within s 51(7)`
            `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate`
            `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person`
            `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province`
            `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission`
            `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder`
            `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)`
            `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65`
            `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77`
    AND (NOT `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes stands in the way`)

§§ `s 51(8) Excepted transmissions`

-- Despite (7), where the law governing the transmission requires no grant of probate or letters of
-- administration or probate of the will or of the notarial minutes, a personal representative of the deceased
-- holder is entitled (subject to tax-collection law) to become a registered holder, or designate one, if they
-- deposit (a) the certificate and (b) reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's
-- interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or their designee.
-- src:847 | Excepted transmissions
-- src:848 | (8) Despite subsection (7), if the laws of the jurisdiction governing the transmission of a security of a deceased holder do not require a grant of probate or of letters of administration or the probate of the will or the notarial minutes of the probate in respect of the transmission, a personal representative of the deceased holder is entitled, subject to any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes, to become a registered holder or to designate a registered holder, if the personal representative deposits with the corporation or its transfer agent
-- src:849 | (a) the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder; and
-- src:850 | (b) reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder’s interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or the person designated by the personal representative to become the registered holder.
@ref CBCA s 51(8) (src:847-850)
GIVEN `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the documents required by subsection 51(8) have been deposited within s 51(8)` MEANS
        `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder`
    AND `the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder`

-- src:847 | Excepted transmissions
-- src:848 | (8) Despite subsection (7), if the laws of the jurisdiction governing the transmission of a security of a deceased holder do not require a grant of probate or of letters of administration or the probate of the will or the notarial minutes of the probate in respect of the transmission, a personal representative of the deceased holder is entitled, subject to any applicable law relating to the collection of taxes, to become a registered holder or to designate a registered holder, if the personal representative deposits with the corporation or its transfer agent
-- src:849 | (a) the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder; and
-- src:850 | (b) reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder’s interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or the person designated by the personal representative to become the registered holder.
@ref CBCA s 51(8) (src:847-850)
GIVEN `the person is a personal representative of the deceased holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws governing the transmission do not require a grant of probate or letters of administration or the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes stands in the way` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the personal representative is entitled to become or designate a registered holder within s 51(8)` MEANS
        `the person is a personal representative of the deceased holder`
    AND `the laws governing the transmission do not require a grant of probate or letters of administration or the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes`
    AND `the documents required by subsection 51(8) have been deposited within s 51(8)`
            `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder`
            `the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder`
    AND (NOT `an applicable law relating to the collection of taxes stands in the way`)

§§ `s 51(9) Right of corporation`

-- Deposit of the documents required by (7) or (8) empowers the corporation or its transfer agent to record
-- the transmission in a securities register and to treat the new registered holder as the owner.
-- src:851 | Right of corporation
-- src:852 | (9) Deposit of the documents required by subsection (7) or (8) empowers a corporation or its transfer agent to record in a securities register the transmission of a security from the deceased holder to a person referred to in paragraph (2)(a) or to such person as the person referred to in that paragraph may designate and, thereafter, to treat the person who thus becomes a registered holder as the owner of those securities.
@ref CBCA s 51(9) (src:851-852)
GIVEN `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation may record the transmission and treat the new registered holder as owner within s 51(9)` MEANS
        `the documents required by subsection 51(7) have been deposited within s 51(7)`
            `the person deposits the original grant of probate or letters of administration or, in Quebec, of the probate of the will or of the notarial minutes of the probate`
            `the person deposits a copy of one of those documents certified true by the court or notary, a trust company incorporated in Canada or a province, or a lawyer or notary acting for the person`
            `in a transmission by notarial will in Quebec the person deposits an authentic copy established in accordance with the laws of that province`
            `the person deposits an affidavit or declaration of transmission stating the particulars of the transmission`
            `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder`
            `the transfer is to a person referred to in paragraph 51(2)(a)`
            `the certificate is endorsed in accordance with section 65`
            `the person gives any assurance the corporation may require under section 77`
    OR  `the documents required by subsection 51(8) have been deposited within s 51(8)`
            `the person deposits the security certificate that was owned by the deceased holder`
            `the person deposits reasonable proof of the governing laws, of the deceased holder's interest or right in the security and of the right of the personal representative or designee to become the registered holder`

§ `s 52 Overissue`

§§ `s 52(1) Overissue`

-- The Part's provisions that validate a security, or compel its issue or reissue, do not apply to the extent
-- that doing so would result in overissue. Instead, (a) if a valid security similar in all respects is
-- reasonably available for purchase, the person entitled may compel the issuer to purchase and deliver
-- one against surrender of the security held; (b) if not, the person may recover from the issuer the price
-- the last purchaser for value paid for the invalid security.
-- src:853 | Overissue
-- src:854 | 52 (1) The provisions of this Part that validate a security or compel its issue or reissue do not apply to the extent that validation, issue or reissue would result in overissue, but
-- src:855 | (a) if a valid security, similar in all respects to the security involved in the overissue, is reasonably available for purchase, the person entitled to the validation or issue may compel the issuer to purchase and deliver such a security against surrender of the security that the person holds;
-- src:856 | (b) if a valid security, similar in all respects to the security involved in the overissue, is not reasonably available for purchase, the person entitled to the validation or issue may recover from the issuer an amount equal to the price the last purchaser for value paid for the invalid security.
@ref CBCA s 52(1) (src:853-856)
DECLARE `Outcome where validation or issue would result in overissue under s 52(1)` IS ONE OF
    `the provisions of this Part apply, because there would be no overissue`
    `the person may compel the issuer to purchase and deliver a similar valid security against surrender of the security held`
    `the person may recover from the issuer the price the last purchaser for value paid for the invalid security` HAS `the amount in dollars` IS A NUMBER

-- src:853 | Overissue
-- src:854 | 52 (1) The provisions of this Part that validate a security or compel its issue or reissue do not apply to the extent that validation, issue or reissue would result in overissue, but
-- src:855 | (a) if a valid security, similar in all respects to the security involved in the overissue, is reasonably available for purchase, the person entitled to the validation or issue may compel the issuer to purchase and deliver such a security against surrender of the security that the person holds;
-- src:856 | (b) if a valid security, similar in all respects to the security involved in the overissue, is not reasonably available for purchase, the person entitled to the validation or issue may recover from the issuer an amount equal to the price the last purchaser for value paid for the invalid security.
@ref CBCA s 52(1) (src:853-856)
GIVEN `validation, issue or reissue would result in overissue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a valid security similar in all respects is reasonably available for purchase` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price the last purchaser for value paid for the invalid security in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Outcome where validation or issue would result in overissue under s 52(1)`
`what the person entitled to validation or issue may do within s 52(1)` MEANS
    IF NOT `validation, issue or reissue would result in overissue`
    THEN `the provisions of this Part apply, because there would be no overissue`
    ELSE IF `a valid security similar in all respects is reasonably available for purchase`
         THEN `the person may compel the issuer to purchase and deliver a similar valid security against surrender of the security held`
         ELSE `the person may recover from the issuer the price the last purchaser for value paid for the invalid security`
                  `the price the last purchaser for value paid for the invalid security in dollars`

§§ `s 52(2) Retroactive validation`

-- When the issuer amends its articles or a trust indenture to which it is a party to raise the authorized
-- number to at least the number previously authorized plus the amount overissued, the overissued securities
-- are valid from the date of their issue.
-- src:857 | Retroactive validation
-- src:858 | (2) When an issuer amends its articles or a trust indenture to which it is a party to increase its authorized securities to a number equal to or in excess of the number of securities previously authorized plus the amount of the securities overissued, the securities so overissued are valid from the date of their issue.
@ref CBCA s 52(2) (src:857-858)
GIVEN `the number of securities authorized after the amendment` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of securities previously authorized` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of securities overissued` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the overissued securities are valid from the date of their issue within s 52(2)` MEANS
    `the number of securities authorized after the amendment`
        AT LEAST (`the number of securities previously authorized` PLUS `the number of securities overissued`)

§§ `s 52(3) Payment not a purchase or redemption`

-- Sections 34, 35, 36 and 39 (out of range: section 34 (piece cb1); section 35 (piece cb1); section 36 (piece cb1); section 39 (piece cb1)) do not apply to a purchase
-- or payment by an issuer under subsection (1). NOTHING: the purchase or payment is not one under (1).
-- src:859 | Payment not a purchase or redemption
-- src:860 | (3) A purchase or payment by an issuer under subsection (1) is not a purchase or payment to which section 34, 35, 36 or 39 applies.
@ref CBCA s 52(3) (src:859-860)
GIVEN `the purchase or payment is made by an issuer under subsection 52(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sections 34, 35, 36 and 39 apply to the purchase or payment within s 52(3)` MEANS
    IF `the purchase or payment is made by an issuer under subsection 52(1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `s 53 Burden of proof`

-- In an action on a security. (a) Each signature on the security or in a necessary endorsement is admitted
-- unless specifically denied in the pleadings.
-- src:861 | Burden of proof
-- src:862 | 53 In an action on a security,
-- src:863 | (a) unless specifically denied in the pleadings, each signature on the security or in a necessary endorsement is admitted;
@ref CBCA s 53(a) (src:861-863)
GIVEN `the action is an action on a security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature is on the security or in a necessary endorsement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature is specifically denied in the pleadings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the signature is admitted within s 53(a)` MEANS
        `the action is an action on a security`
    AND `the signature is on the security or in a necessary endorsement`
    AND (NOT `the signature is specifically denied in the pleadings`)

-- (b) A signature on the security is presumed to be genuine and authorized; but if the effectiveness of
-- the signature is put in issue, the burden of establishing that it is genuine and authorized is on the
-- party claiming under the signature.
-- src:861 | Burden of proof
-- src:862 | 53 In an action on a security,
-- src:863 | (a) unless specifically denied in the pleadings, each signature on the security or in a necessary endorsement is admitted;
-- src:864 | (b) a signature on the security is presumed to be genuine and authorized but, if the effectiveness of the signature is put in issue, the burden of establishing that it is genuine and authorized is on the party claiming under the signature;
@ref CBCA s 53(b) (src:861-864)
GIVEN `the action is an action on a security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature is on the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the signature is presumed to be genuine and authorized within s 53(b)` MEANS
        `the action is an action on a security`
    AND `the signature is on the security`

-- src:861 | Burden of proof
-- src:862 | 53 In an action on a security,
-- src:863 | (a) unless specifically denied in the pleadings, each signature on the security or in a necessary endorsement is admitted;
-- src:864 | (b) a signature on the security is presumed to be genuine and authorized but, if the effectiveness of the signature is put in issue, the burden of establishing that it is genuine and authorized is on the party claiming under the signature;
@ref CBCA s 53(b) (src:861-864)
GIVEN `the action is an action on a security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature is on the security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the effectiveness of the signature is put in issue` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the party claiming under the signature bears the burden of establishing that it is genuine and authorized within s 53(b)` MEANS
        `the action is an action on a security`
    AND `the signature is on the security`
    AND `the effectiveness of the signature is put in issue`

-- (c) If a signature is admitted or established, production of the instrument entitles a holder to recover
-- on it unless the defendant establishes a defence or a defect going to the validity of the security.
-- src:861 | Burden of proof
-- src:862 | 53 In an action on a security,
-- src:863 | (a) unless specifically denied in the pleadings, each signature on the security or in a necessary endorsement is admitted;
-- src:864 | (b) a signature on the security is presumed to be genuine and authorized but, if the effectiveness of the signature is put in issue, the burden of establishing that it is genuine and authorized is on the party claiming under the signature;
-- src:865 | (c) if a signature is admitted or established, production of the instrument entitles a holder to recover on it unless the defendant establishes a defence or a defect going to the validity of the security; and
@ref CBCA s 53(c) (src:861-865)
GIVEN `the action is an action on a security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a signature is admitted or established` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument is produced by a holder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant establishes a defence or a defect going to the validity of the security` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`production of the instrument entitles the holder to recover within s 53(c)` MEANS
        `the action is an action on a security`
    AND `a signature is admitted or established`
    AND `the instrument is produced by a holder`
    AND (NOT `the defendant establishes a defence or a defect going to the validity of the security`)

-- (d) If the defendant establishes that a defence or defect exists, the plaintiff has the burden of
-- establishing that it is ineffective against the plaintiff or some person under whom the plaintiff claims.
-- src:861 | Burden of proof
-- src:862 | 53 In an action on a security,
-- src:863 | (a) unless specifically denied in the pleadings, each signature on the security or in a necessary endorsement is admitted;
-- src:864 | (b) a signature on the security is presumed to be genuine and authorized but, if the effectiveness of the signature is put in issue, the burden of establishing that it is genuine and authorized is on the party claiming under the signature;
-- src:865 | (c) if a signature is admitted or established, production of the instrument entitles a holder to recover on it unless the defendant establishes a defence or a defect going to the validity of the security; and
-- src:866 | (d) if the defendant establishes that a defence or defect exists, the plaintiff has the burden of establishing that the defence or defect is ineffective against the plaintiff or some person under whom the plaintiff claims.
@ref CBCA s 53(d) (src:861-866)
GIVEN `the action is an action on a security` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant establishes that a defence or defect exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the plaintiff bears the burden of establishing that the defence or defect is ineffective within s 53(d)` MEANS
        `the action is an action on a security`
    AND `the defendant establishes that a defence or defect exists`

§ `s 54 Securities fungible`

-- Unless otherwise agreed, and subject to this Act, any other applicable Act of Parliament or of a
-- provincial legislature, any applicable regulation, and any applicable stock exchange rule, a person
-- required to deliver securities may deliver any security of the specified issue.
-- src:867 | Securities fungible
-- src:868 | 54 Unless otherwise agreed and subject to the provisions of this Act, of any other applicable Act of Parliament, of any applicable Act of the legislature of a province or of any applicable regulation made under any such Act or to any applicable stock exchange rule, a person required to deliver securities may deliver any security of the specified issue.
@ref CBCA s 54 (src:867-868)
GIVEN `the person is required to deliver securities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the security delivered is of the specified issue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision of this Act, of another applicable Act, of an applicable regulation or an applicable stock exchange rule requires otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may deliver any security of the specified issue within s 54` MEANS
        `the person is required to deliver securities`
    AND `the security delivered is of the specified issue`
    AND (NOT `the parties otherwise agreed`)
    AND (NOT `a provision of this Act, of another applicable Act, of an applicable regulation or an applicable stock exchange rule requires otherwise`)
